WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.311
Quiz maker turns notes into practice.

00:00:04.311 --> 00:00:08.162
This walkthrough uses public sample notes and a demo provider.

00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:12.784
Open a note, then use the command palette to choose Quick quiz.

00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:15.480
To write questions yourself, choose New quiz.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.866
The current note is selected for you.

00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:20.318
Choose a study pack and a question mix.

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:24.304
Keep the defaults for a quick start, or open the optional controls when

00:00:24.304 --> 00:00:25.224
you need them.

00:00:25.464 --> 00:00:28.414
In settings, choose your provider and endpoint.

00:00:28.414 --> 00:00:31.785
Add an API key for a hosted provider.

00:00:31.785 --> 00:00:35.999
Find models checks the connection and loads the available list.

00:00:35.999 --> 00:00:38.106
Search, then select a model.

00:00:38.106 --> 00:00:40.213
Manual model IDs remain available.

00:00:40.454 --> 00:00:41.682
Generate your quiz.

00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:45.368
Only the selected notes go to the configured provider.

00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:49.873
Review generated questions and reference answers against your source before studying.

00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:53.327
Answer a question, check your response, and move on.

00:00:53.327 --> 00:00:57.970
Choose an exam when you want a timer and answers hidden until submission.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.113
Your progress stays in the vault.

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:03.718
The mini view shares the same session beside your notes.

00:01:03.718 --> 00:01:06.746
Use the full view when you want more space.

00:01:06.746 --> 00:01:09.102
Quiz appearance can follow your Obsidian theme.

00:01:09.342 --> 00:01:12.233
Edit questions and undo changes when needed.

00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:15.125
Export JSON, Anki cards, or a PDF.

00:01:15.125 --> 00:01:18.842
Saved packs and preferences stay in place across updates.

00:01:18.842 --> 00:01:22.146
The written guide is linked in the repository.
